# Anything listed here is kept out of the packaged VSIX. Note this is a
# SEPARATE list from .gitignore and the two diverge in opposite directions:
#
#   - A git-IGNORED file reaches a local `npm run package` if it is sitting in
#     the tree. CI starts from a clean checkout, so it only ships one the build
#     itself creates -- `dist/` is git-ignored and IS published, which is why
#     "git-ignored means CI-safe" is wrong.
#   - A git-TRACKED file is shipped by CI unconditionally. Those are the ones
#     that leak without anyone doing something unusual.
#
# So internal notes that live in the repo must be listed here explicitly, and
# secrets must be listed here too in case someone packages from a dirty tree.
src/
.planning/
.claude/
.crash-buffers/
CRASH-BUFFER.md
HANDOFF-*.md
.env
.env.*
out/
*.vsix
node_modules/
.git/
.gitignore
tsconfig.json
esbuild.config.mjs
jest.config.*
**/*.map
.vscode/
.eslintrc.json
**/*.test.ts
**/__tests__/
build.ps1
compile.ps1
CLAUDE.md
dev/
coverage/
.mcp.json
PUBLISHING.md
renovate.json
biome.json
.github/
